# Monthly estimates: one representative resource per target and taxonomy category

One row per target and taxonomy category the target's embedded snapshot offers, through
`assessment.AssessWith` with estimates on (the path `shift2eu assess` takes), never through a
rendered report. The plan is the cheapest covering plan the estimate chose, the amount is the
monthly list price in EUR rounded to the cent, and a resource that is not estimated gives its
reason instead. Regenerate with `go test ./test/examples -update`.

Sizes, chosen for this table within PRD #190's sizing fields (inventory format version 2,
ADR 0025): a virtual machine is 2 vCPU, 4 GiB of memory, count 1 and 730 hours a month; a
bare-metal server is 4 vCPU and 32 GiB, the smallest plan OVHcloud's and Scaleway's bare-metal
offerings cover (UpCloud offers none); Kubernetes counts 3 nodes of the virtual-machine size; a
managed database is 2 vCPU, 4 GiB of memory and 50 GiB of storage; block storage is one 100 GiB
volume and object storage 100 GiB stored; a function is 1 GiB of memory; a queue takes no size.
A MongoDB database is 2 vCPU, 8 GiB of memory, 100 GiB of storage and count 3, the nodes of a
replica set; a search cluster and a Kafka cluster are the same size, 2 vCPU, 8 GiB of memory
and 100 GiB of storage per node at count 3, with no capability, so they are priced on the 1-AZ
tier the default region serves; a cache is 6 GiB of memory per node, count 2 and
`node-high-availability`, so it is priced on the multi-node tier a replicated cache is served
by, and its capability is shown after its size; a load balancer and a container registry take
no size and are not priced.

- `OVHcloud`: prices retrieved 2026-11-27 from `https://www.ovhcloud.com/en-ie/public-cloud/prices/`, estimated in `GRA` (its default region)
- `Scaleway`: prices retrieved 2026-11-13 from `https://www.scaleway.com/en/pricing/`, estimated in `fr-par` (its default region)
- `UpCloud`: prices retrieved 2026-11-13 from `https://upcloud.com/pricing/`, estimated in `de-fra1` (its default region)

